; The parent: signed, and vouched for by the trust anchor the scenario
; builds from the key clove generates for it.
;
; The delegation below carries a DS, so the child is a secure one and
; the resolver is expected to check what it sends.  The DS is made up,
; though, and matches no key the child has, which is what
; dnssec-failed.mufj.jp is: a zone whose chain of trust is broken at the
; first step.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.example.
ns		IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
www		IN	A	192.0.2.1
bogus		IN	NS	ns.bogus.example.
ns.bogus	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
bogus		IN	DS	12345 15 2 0102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f20
